{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Place now your hand under my thigh.</b> Some say it hints at circumcision. If so, he would have sworn by the covenant of circumcision and not by the Name. It seems closer to me that it was a custom in those days for a man to place his hand under the thigh of one who was under his authority. The meaning is: if you are under my authority, place now your hand under my thigh. The master sits and the thigh is over the hand, in the sense of: behold, my hand is under your authority to do your will. This custom still exists in the land of India."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:32.542080702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}